                <pb facs="0604" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg598"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Newport</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my telegram of to day and
                    to your note of the 9th instant, I have the honor to inform you that I have
                    received a telegram from my Government in which it is stated that the German
                    Government is ready to take charge of Mataafa and eleven other chiefs and keep
                    them in the Marshall Islands. They propose at the same time that the three
                    powers divide the cost of their keep. Her Majesty’s Government hope that the
                    United States Government will approve of this proposal in which they concur.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
